WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.500 --> 00:00:03.317
Welcome to The Fantastical Logic Grid.

2
00:00:03.667 --> 00:00:07.806
Every case is a brand new story, and you are
the detective.

3
00:00:08.856 --> 00:00:12.185
Each puzzle is a logic grid wrapped in a
story.

4
00:00:12.535 --> 00:00:16.203
The story sets up a mystery, the clues give
you the facts,

5
00:00:16.223 --> 00:00:19.298
and the grid is where you work out the answer.

6
00:00:20.348 --> 00:00:24.423
Every story is written fresh for you and never
repeated.

7
00:00:24.773 --> 00:00:29.595
And every puzzle has exactly one answer you
can reach without guessing.

8
00:00:30.645 --> 00:00:35.318
New to logic puzzles? Press How to play, at
the top of every page.

9
00:00:35.668 --> 00:00:39.786
It teaches you to solve them step by step, on
real grids.

10
00:00:40.836 --> 00:00:47.087
Five short lessons take you from your very
first mark to solving a whole puzzle on your
own.

11
00:00:47.437 --> 00:00:49.309
They cover every kind of clue,

12
00:00:49.329 --> 00:00:53.262
carrying facts across the grid, what-if
thinking, and hints.

13
00:00:54.312 --> 00:00:58.729
Each step explains one idea, then you make the
marks yourself.

14
00:00:59.079 --> 00:01:01.623
The game tells you when a mark does not fit,

15
00:01:01.643 --> 00:01:04.882
and Show me makes the marks for you if you are
stuck.

16
00:01:05.932 --> 00:01:10.391
Tips and tricks puts the moves that solve most
puzzles on one page.

17
00:01:11.441 --> 00:01:16.364
In a hurry? Play a quick puzzle starts a small
Easy case straight away,

18
00:01:16.384 --> 00:01:18.205
with no choices to make.

19
00:01:19.255 --> 00:01:24.226
Every day there is also a new Daily puzzle,
the same one for everyone.

20
00:01:24.576 --> 00:01:27.030
Solve it each day to build a streak.

21
00:01:28.080 --> 00:01:32.241
With a free sign-in, you can get each day's
puzzle by email.

22
00:01:33.291 --> 00:01:36.669
Every Monday there is also a Puzzle of the
week:

23
00:01:36.689 --> 00:01:40.097
a bigger Expert puzzle with a brand-new story.

24
00:01:41.147 --> 00:01:46.120
Anyone can get the puzzle of the week and
special edition puzzles by email,

25
00:01:46.140 --> 00:01:47.355
with no account.

26
00:01:47.705 --> 00:01:51.152
Choose Puzzle emails in the Menu, type your
address,

27
00:01:51.172 --> 00:01:54.255
then press Confirm in the email we send you.

28
00:01:55.305 --> 00:01:56.949
Here's how to play.

29
00:01:57.999 --> 00:02:01.541
Start on the New puzzle screen and pick a
difficulty.

30
00:02:01.891 --> 00:02:05.006
Basic and Easy are perfect for beginners.

31
00:02:05.356 --> 00:02:08.429
Quantum Physicist is for true masterminds.

32
00:02:08.779 --> 00:02:12.577
And Theoretical Physicist is for the best of
the best.

33
00:02:13.627 --> 00:02:16.384
Next, choose a theme. Themes are grouped,

34
00:02:16.404 --> 00:02:20.753
like Mystery and Action, Imagination, or
Science and Learning.

35
00:02:21.103 --> 00:02:22.917
Or pick Surprise me.

36
00:02:23.967 --> 00:02:27.949
Most themes also open a list of topics right
under them,

37
00:02:27.969 --> 00:02:31.263
like which holiday or which kind of mystery.

38
00:02:31.613 --> 00:02:33.662
Pick one, or leave it on Any.

39
00:02:34.712 --> 00:02:36.291
Then pick a size.

40
00:02:36.641 --> 00:02:40.759
More categories and more items make a bigger,
harder grid.

41
00:02:41.809 --> 00:02:46.802
Under More options, Full experience adds
scenes, characters and sound.

42
00:02:47.152 --> 00:02:52.187
Silent mode keeps only the story, the grid,
the clues and the answer key.

43
00:02:53.237 --> 00:02:57.313
Press Generate puzzle, and your story is
written in a moment.

44
00:02:58.363 --> 00:03:01.713
Here's our case: The Topsy-Turvy Red Nose.

45
00:03:02.063 --> 00:03:05.178
The buttons along the top help you as you
play.

46
00:03:06.228 --> 00:03:07.978
Read the story first.

47
00:03:08.328 --> 00:03:13.577
It tells you who is involved, and it ends with
the question you need to answer.

48
00:03:13.927 --> 00:03:17.106
Here, it's: Who went on at 7:30 PM?

49
00:03:17.456 --> 00:03:20.870
You can also press Read the story aloud to
hear it.

50
00:03:21.920 --> 00:03:27.659
Every character has a personality, shown under
their name, and a voice of their own.

51
00:03:28.009 --> 00:03:33.237
Select a character's portrait to hear the
clues they remember, in their own words.

52
00:03:33.587 --> 00:03:36.233
Every clue is also in the clue list.

53
00:03:37.283 --> 00:03:41.251
To hear every clue in order, press Read the
clues aloud.

54
00:03:41.601 --> 00:03:46.338
Each character tells their own clue, and the
clue being read lights up.

55
00:03:47.388 --> 00:03:53.319
On your first Easy puzzle, coach tips appear
above the grid to guide your first moves.

56
00:03:54.369 --> 00:03:55.735
Now the grid.

57
00:03:56.085 --> 00:04:00.566
Each square is where two things meet, like a
performer and a showtime.

58
00:04:00.916 --> 00:04:04.309
Your job is to decide whether they go
together.

59
00:04:05.359 --> 00:04:08.303
Click or tap a square once to mark an X.

60
00:04:08.653 --> 00:04:12.110
X means ruled out: these two don't go
together.

61
00:04:13.160 --> 00:04:17.470
Tap again for an O. O means confirmed: these
two are a match.

62
00:04:17.820 --> 00:04:20.295
Tap a third time to clear the square.

63
00:04:21.345 --> 00:04:25.207
Let's solve it together, starting with the
simplest clues.

64
00:04:25.557 --> 00:04:28.779
Clues 1 and 2 each rule out pairs directly.

65
00:04:29.129 --> 00:04:31.093
Mark an X for each one.

66
00:04:32.143 --> 00:04:35.450
Clue 3 says Gwendolyn performs the Trapeze.

67
00:04:35.800 --> 00:04:37.337
Mark an O there.

68
00:04:38.387 --> 00:04:42.419
Clue 4 says Gwendolyn went on at 7:30 PM.

69
00:04:42.769 --> 00:04:44.306
Mark an O there.

70
00:04:45.356 --> 00:04:52.013
Clue 5 says the performer who performs the
Juggling did not go on at 7:50 PM.

71
00:04:52.363 --> 00:04:53.985
Mark an X there.

72
00:04:55.035 --> 00:04:58.662
Clue 6 says Celeste went on at 7:50 PM.

73
00:04:59.012 --> 00:05:00.549
Mark an O there.

74
00:05:01.599 --> 00:05:06.922
Gwendolyn performs the Trapeze, so Gwendolyn
cannot go with any other act,

75
00:05:06.942 --> 00:05:10.197
and no other performer can go with Trapeze.

76
00:05:10.547 --> 00:05:14.840
Each row and each column in a section has
exactly one match,

77
00:05:14.860 --> 00:05:17.886
so everything else in that line is an X.

78
00:05:18.936 --> 00:05:25.051
Celeste went on at 7:50 PM, so Celeste cannot
go with any other showtime,

79
00:05:25.071 --> 00:05:28.835
and no other performer can go with 7:50 PM.

80
00:05:29.885 --> 00:05:36.368
Gwendolyn went on at 7:30 PM, so Gwendolyn
cannot go with any other showtime,

81
00:05:36.388 --> 00:05:40.169
and no other performer can go with 7:30 PM.

82
00:05:41.219 --> 00:05:44.462
Acrobatics is the only act left for Anouk.

83
00:05:44.812 --> 00:05:46.349
Mark an O there.

84
00:05:46.699 --> 00:05:51.798
When only one square is left in a row or
column, it must be the answer.

85
00:05:52.848 --> 00:05:58.161
In the full experience, each finished section
also reveals more of the scene.

86
00:05:59.211 --> 00:06:00.769
Stuck? Press Hint.

87
00:06:01.119 --> 00:06:06.069
The first hint shows you which clue to use,
and names the trick that cracks it.

88
00:06:07.119 --> 00:06:12.389
Press Which cell? for the exact square, then
Explain why for the full reasoning.

89
00:06:12.739 --> 00:06:16.195
It ends with a short lesson on how that trick
works,

90
00:06:16.215 --> 00:06:18.905
so you can spot it yourself next time.

91
00:06:19.255 --> 00:06:22.199
You can even let it mark the square for you.

92
00:06:23.249 --> 00:06:27.431
Press Check at any time to see whether any of
your marks are wrong.

93
00:06:28.481 --> 00:06:33.986
Made a mistake? Undo and Redo take back any
move, as many times as you like.

94
00:06:35.036 --> 00:06:38.002
Want a fresh start? Press Start over.

95
00:06:38.352 --> 00:06:42.321
It clears your marks and resets the timer,
hints and checks.

96
00:06:42.671 --> 00:06:48.239
Your notes stay unless you choose to clear
them, and Undo can bring everything back.

97
00:06:49.289 --> 00:06:54.218
Prefer words to grids? List view lets you
choose each match from a menu.

98
00:06:54.568 --> 00:06:58.601
The game also works fully by keyboard and with
a screen reader.

99
00:06:59.651 --> 00:07:04.750
When you think you know, answer the questions
under the clues, and press Check answers.

100
00:07:05.800 --> 00:07:09.491
Want to jot something down? Press My notes and
type.

101
00:07:09.841 --> 00:07:13.703
Press Save to keep them, or Close to get back
to the puzzle.

102
00:07:14.053 --> 00:07:17.190
Only you can see your notes, even in a race.

103
00:07:18.240 --> 00:07:23.083
Keep going the same way, clue by clue, until
the whole grid is filled in.

104
00:07:24.133 --> 00:07:25.457
Case closed!

105
00:07:25.807 --> 00:07:28.181
Gwendolyn went on at 7:30 PM.

106
00:07:28.201 --> 00:07:33.551
Gwendolyn bows to the crowd and hands back the
famous red nose.

107
00:07:33.901 --> 00:07:38.062
You also see your time and a suggestion for
your next puzzle.

108
00:07:39.112 --> 00:07:42.822
Every solve ends with a celebration, like
confetti,

109
00:07:42.842 --> 00:07:46.430
fireworks, ribbons, balloons or shooting
stars.

110
00:07:46.780 --> 00:07:51.389
Silent mode and your device's reduce motion
setting turn it off.

111
00:07:52.439 --> 00:07:56.237
Solving puzzles earns badges, like First case
closed.

112
00:07:56.587 --> 00:08:00.504
Press Share my result to send friends a
picture of your win.

113
00:08:00.524 --> 00:08:02.774
It never gives the answers away.

114
00:08:03.824 --> 00:08:08.753
Challenge a friend makes a link to this very
puzzle, with your time to beat.

115
00:08:09.103 --> 00:08:13.135
Your friend needs no account, and you both see
who was quicker.

116
00:08:14.185 --> 00:08:19.317
If you like, rate the puzzle from 1 to 5
stars, where 5 is excellent,

117
00:08:19.337 --> 00:08:23.743
and say whether it felt too easy, just right
or too hard.

118
00:08:24.093 --> 00:08:25.062
It is optional.

119
00:08:25.082 --> 00:08:30.046
The game learns from your answers and tunes
your next puzzle to suit you.

120
00:08:31.096 --> 00:08:37.113
You can print any puzzle, blank or with your
marks, with the answer key on its own page.

121
00:08:38.163 --> 00:08:40.659
Your progress saves automatically.

122
00:08:41.009 --> 00:08:45.746
Come back any time and pick up where you left
off, from Saved puzzles.

123
00:08:46.796 --> 00:08:51.305
My stats and badges, in the Menu, shows your
totals, best times,

124
00:08:51.325 --> 00:08:55.650
favorite themes, your daily streak and every
badge to earn.

125
00:08:56.700 --> 00:08:59.538
Press Help to see every keyboard shortcut.

126
00:09:00.588 --> 00:09:05.346
And Introduction, at the top of every page,
plays this video again.

127
00:09:06.396 --> 00:09:08.573
Play in light or dark colors,

128
00:09:09.623 --> 00:09:11.501
or in high contrast.

129
00:09:12.551 --> 00:09:16.839
And Silent mode is always there when you just
want the puzzle.

130
00:09:17.889 --> 00:09:23.885
To play without opening a browser, choose
Install the app on The Logic Grid home page.

131
00:09:24.235 --> 00:09:28.737
Download the Windows desktop app, which keeps
itself up to date.

132
00:09:29.087 --> 00:09:32.773
Or add the game's icon to your phone's home
screen.

133
00:09:32.793 --> 00:09:36.213
On your phone, the same button shows you how.

134
00:09:36.563 --> 00:09:42.729
On a phone, pull down from the top of the page
to refresh. Your progress is saved first.

135
00:09:43.779 --> 00:09:46.446
You can also play with other detectives.

136
00:09:47.496 --> 00:09:52.260
You can play as a guest, with a few new
puzzles a day in every game,

137
00:09:52.280 --> 00:09:56.158
plus the daily puzzle, saved puzzles and How
to play.

138
00:09:56.508 --> 00:10:01.104
A free account gives you unlimited puzzles,
and keeps your puzzles,

139
00:10:01.124 --> 00:10:06.578
progress and settings in step on the website,
the desktop app and your phone.

140
00:10:07.628 --> 00:10:10.658
The name at the top shows who you are playing
as.

141
00:10:11.008 --> 00:10:13.718
Until you sign in, you play as Guest.

142
00:10:14.768 --> 00:10:20.081
Race the computer pits you against a computer
player on a brand new puzzle.

143
00:10:20.431 --> 00:10:22.009
Pick how fast it plays,

144
00:10:22.029 --> 00:10:26.767
and the race bar shows how far along it is.
Solve it first to win.

145
00:10:27.817 --> 00:10:30.570
Create one with your email and a password.

146
00:10:30.920 --> 00:10:35.618
Keep me signed in is ticked, so you stay
signed in on this device.

147
00:10:35.638 --> 00:10:38.003
Untick it on a shared computer.

148
00:10:38.353 --> 00:10:43.559
If you ever forget your password, Forgot
password sends you a reset link.

149
00:10:44.609 --> 00:10:48.322
Once you are signed in, your puzzles sync on
their own.

150
00:10:48.672 --> 00:10:52.406
Sign in on another device and they are waiting
for you.

151
00:10:53.456 --> 00:10:59.063
Signed in, Printable puzzle pack in the Menu
prints a few brand-new puzzles at once,

152
00:10:59.083 --> 00:11:00.774
with their answer keys.

153
00:11:01.124 --> 00:11:04.191
Pick how many, the difficulty and the theme.

154
00:11:04.211 --> 00:11:07.589
Each player gets a set number of packs a week.

155
00:11:08.639 --> 00:11:11.839
Once you are signed in, you pick a screen
name.

156
00:11:12.189 --> 00:11:16.926
Type your own, or press Suggest a name and the
game makes one up for you.

157
00:11:17.276 --> 00:11:22.119
It is the only thing other players see, and
rude names are turned away.

158
00:11:22.469 --> 00:11:26.225
Don't want one? Sign out instead, and you play
as Guest.

159
00:11:27.275 --> 00:11:29.942
Your screen name now shows at the top.

160
00:11:30.292 --> 00:11:35.260
Play against others lets you race other
players on the very same puzzle,

161
00:11:35.280 --> 00:11:37.162
and climb the scoreboard.

162
00:11:38.212 --> 00:11:40.325
To race, press Start a race.

163
00:11:40.675 --> 00:11:46.073
It uses the difficulty, theme and size you
picked on the New puzzle screen.

164
00:11:47.123 --> 00:11:49.961
Share the race code or link with a friend.

165
00:11:50.311 --> 00:11:54.215
Or anyone can press Find a race to join an
open race.

166
00:11:55.265 --> 00:11:57.783
Everyone gets the very same puzzle.

167
00:11:58.133 --> 00:12:02.934
The race bar shows the code, and Standings
shows who is still solving.

168
00:12:03.984 --> 00:12:06.353
When you finish, you see your place.

169
00:12:06.703 --> 00:12:10.309
Fastest solve wins, and each hint adds time.

170
00:12:11.359 --> 00:12:14.965
The scoreboard ranks players this week and of
all time.

171
00:12:15.315 --> 00:12:19.283
Every solve earns points, even when you play
on your own.

172
00:12:19.633 --> 00:12:24.199
Press Scoring and race rules to see exactly
how points are awarded.

173
00:12:25.249 --> 00:12:29.346
This week's leaders are always in view at the
top of the page.

174
00:12:29.696 --> 00:12:32.385
Select Scoreboard there to see the full board.

175
00:12:33.435 --> 00:12:38.939
To race one particular player, press Challenge
a player and type their screen name.

176
00:12:39.989 --> 00:12:45.366
They see your challenge under Play against
others, the next time they open the game.

177
00:12:45.716 --> 00:12:50.901
Accept starts the race on the very same
puzzle. No thanks turns it down.

178
00:12:51.951 --> 00:12:54.085
Finally, make the game your own.

179
00:12:55.135 --> 00:13:01.066
In Settings, sound effects and theme music
start on, and you can turn either one off.

180
00:13:01.416 --> 00:13:05.150
Learn from how I play tunes your next puzzles
to suit you.

181
00:13:06.200 --> 00:13:08.227
And play in your own language.

182
00:13:08.577 --> 00:13:15.191
US English is the default, and you can choose
any of 100 languages under Language.

183
00:13:15.541 --> 00:13:18.137
The game translates itself as you play,

184
00:13:18.157 --> 00:13:22.667
and the English button at the top shows the
original at any time.

185
00:13:23.717 --> 00:13:26.601
When the team writes to you, or posts news,

186
00:13:26.621 --> 00:13:31.227
you see a number on the Menu button in the
desktop and phone apps.

187
00:13:32.277 --> 00:13:35.711
Messages and news, on The Logic Grid home
page,

188
00:13:35.731 --> 00:13:39.041
has news from the game's team for everyone.

189
00:13:39.391 --> 00:13:43.126
Signed in, you can write to the team with a
question,

190
00:13:43.146 --> 00:13:47.263
an idea or a problem, and read their replies
right here.

191
00:13:47.613 --> 00:13:51.945
Tick Email me, and you get a short email when
the team writes back.

192
00:13:52.995 --> 00:13:57.710
Dream up a character of your own with Suggest
a character, in the menu.

193
00:13:58.060 --> 00:14:03.095
Answer a few questions about their name, look,
personality and voice.

194
00:14:03.445 --> 00:14:08.737
The game's team reviews every suggestion, and
you might meet yours in a puzzle.

195
00:14:09.787 --> 00:14:12.283
Want to write a whole puzzle of your own?

196
00:14:12.633 --> 00:14:16.751
Submit Puzzle Ideas, in the menu, walks you
through your story,

197
00:14:16.771 --> 00:14:20.271
your characters, the lists to match and the
answer.

198
00:14:20.621 --> 00:14:24.244
It checks that your puzzle has exactly one
answer,

199
00:14:24.264 --> 00:14:29.731
gives you a PDF to download or print, and
saves it to your Saved puzzles.

200
00:14:30.781 --> 00:14:36.329
That's all you need: read the story, follow
the clues, and mark your X's and O's.

201
00:14:36.679 --> 00:14:40.797
Welcome to The Fantastical Logic Grid. Happy
sleuthing!

